{
  "category": "Brutal Star Pokémon",
  "entries": [
    {
      "text": "It plunges the poison spike on its head into its prey. When the prey has weakened, Mareanie deals the finishing blow with its 10 tentacles.",
      "version": "sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "It’s found crawling on beaches and seafloors. The coral that grows on Corsola’s head is as good as a five-star banquet to this Pokémon.",
      "version": "moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "They eat Corsola branches, so Mareanie are hated by craftsmen who work with Corsola branches that have naturally fallen off.",
      "version": "ultra-sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "Aside from its head, its body parts regenerate quickly if they’re cut off. After a good night’s sleep, Mareanie is back to normal.",
      "version": "ultra-moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "The first symptom of its sting is numbness. The next is an itching sensation so intense that it’s impossible to resist the urge to claw at your skin.",
      "version": "sword"
    },
    {
      "text": "Unlike their Alolan counterparts, the Mareanie of the Galar region have not yet figured out that the branches of Corsola are delicious.",
      "version": "shield"
    }
  ],
